# File: tests/blender/test_estimate_landmarks.py
# Generated from: specs/137-add-estimate-landmarks-to-propose-rig-humanoid-landmarks-from-the-mesh/requirements.md
Feature: estimate_landmarks proposes rig_humanoid landmarks from the mesh

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Landmarks are proposed for an A-pose humanoid
    Given a symmetric A-pose humanoid with known joint positions
    When the agent calls estimate_landmarks
    Then the result is ok with high confidence, no warnings, and all 19 landmarks
    And each landmark is within 5% of the height of its known joint
    And every _l landmark has x > 0 and every _r landmark has x < 0

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A high-confidence proposal rigs without edits
    Given the landmarks from a high confidence result
    When they are passed unchanged to rig_humanoid
    Then rig_humanoid returns ok

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Stylized proportions and accessories do not mislead it
    Given a stylized A-pose character with a large head and a hat brim, earrings, or glasses
    When the agent calls estimate_landmarks
    Then the shoulders are placed at the arms, not at the accessory
    And the result meets the A-pose checks

  @SCN004
  Scenario: An asymmetric stance is reported as low confidence
    Given an A-pose humanoid whose arms or legs are not mirrored within 5% of its height
    When the agent calls estimate_landmarks
    Then the result is ok with low confidence
    And the landmarks are measured per side, not mirror-averaged
    And warnings name each asymmetric pair

  @SCN005
  Scenario: No A-pose arms or no crotch is a failure
    Given a T-pose humanoid, a humanoid with arms fused to the torso, or a mesh with no crotch
    When the agent calls estimate_landmarks
    Then the result is rig.arms_not_found or rig.crotch_not_found with a message and a remediation
    And it has no landmarks

  @SCN006
  Scenario: A missing mesh is reported
    Given a missing collection or a collection without SM_<Name>
    When the agent calls estimate_landmarks
    Then the result is rig.asset_not_found naming the expected mesh

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Estimating changes nothing
    Given any collection
    When estimate_landmarks returns with any status
    Then objects, mesh data, transforms, selection, active object, and mode are unchanged

  @SCN008
  Scenario: rig_humanoid uses the mesh's current position
    Given SM_<Name> moved, rotated, and scaled in a script with no view-layer update
    When the script calls rig_humanoid with landmarks for the new position
    Then rig_humanoid returns ok
    And estimate_landmarks returns landmarks at the new position

  @SCN009
  Scenario: rig_humanoid messages name the mesh
    Given a collection Hero
    When rig_humanoid fails with rig.asset_not_found, rig.landmarks_outside_mesh, or rig.weights_failed
    Then the message and remediation say SM_Hero and Hero
    And no result contains SM_<Name> or <Name>

  @SCN010
  Scenario: The agent flow is documented
    Given docs/rigging-and-animation.md
    When an agent reads the flow
    Then it calls estimate_landmarks, reviews and corrects the proposal, and then calls rig_humanoid
    And the result fields, confidence values, A-pose limit, and failure codes are documented
